 ## Background
-The Splat Attributes Pass originates from the field of point-based rendering and Gaussian Splatting, where 3D primitives are projected onto the 2D screen and rendered as fragments. The specific technique of using depth-based occlusion and radial/depth-proximity weighting for attribute accumulation was detailed in unofficial implementations such as `arminkz/PointCloudRendering` [S1, unofficial]. It builds on the principles of object-order rendering, where splats are processed in screen space order, and has been adapted for real-time rendering of large point clouds and Gaussian splats. The method is commonly used in real-time viewers for 3D Gaussian Splatting and point cloud visualization tools [S1, unofficial].
